    "body": "Add one regression proving that an expected-state mismatch returns failure while retaining the complete actual aggregate and all ten expanded stage reports. One existing test file changes; production and frozen expectations are unchanged.\n\nValidation on integration7498ffb1: selected Rust regression passed58.519s, with one existing positive test filtered. The inner CLI failure and complete outputs are asserted in memory; no separate raw inner-process capture is claimed.\n\nFresh whole current source/result review is pending. This draft is stacked after the Source/6 rebate integration.\n\n\n### Current source and result review\n\nFresh review of exact head `7498ffb15323ba85ccb97135c994a9a8214e041e` and its actual result is now qualified and adopted. The selected Rust regression passed in 58.519 seconds, with one existing test filtered. The inner CLI failure, complete aggregate and ten expanded reports are asserted in memory; they were not separately captured as raw output. This adds reporting regression coverage, with no financial-oracle or production behavior change.\n\nThe exact published stack still requires parent delivery and verified main-tree equality before merge. No wider EARS, native or target exit is closed by this PR.\n",
